# One CI gate, one file. Issue #991 moved the gate list out of
# `.github/workflows/release.yml` so two branches adding gates create two
# files, never one shared region. `rust-script scripts/run-ci-gates.rs
# --stage <stage>` runs them.
#
# Issue #1047 measured what `cargo nextest --partition slice:N/D` costs. It
# splits by test index, which is uncorrelated with duration -- across run
# 32591020809 (2895 tests, 4704s of work over eight slices) index order gave a
# 870s worst slice against a 588s ideal, so the critical path waited 282s on
# one machine while the others sat idle. Longest-processing-time-first reaches
# 588s exactly.
#
# This gate fails when the planned partitions drift back out of balance, which
# is what happens silently as tests are added and the recorded durations go
# stale. A rebalance is a re-recording, not a code change.
ci_gate check_test_partition_balance
  stage rust
  description "Long tests start first so the planned test partitions stay balanced."
  run "rust-script scripts/plan-test-partition.rs --report --of 8"
